🎛️ Layer 1: Dynamic Sovereignty (L49–L52)
The Problem It Solves
Without sovereignty nodes, Lucy proposes → human rejects → Lucy proposes the same thing again. The human becomes a passenger in their own project.

The Mechanism
Rejection tracking:

user rejects proposal once → confidenceThreshold: 0.85 → 0.75
user rejects proposal twice → confidenceThreshold: 0.75 → 0.65 + SCAFFOLDING ACTIVATED
user queries "why" twice → confidenceThreshold: additional -0.05
user takes manual control → confidenceThreshold: -0.15 + SCAFFOLDING ACTIVATED
Scaffolding Mode — 5 graduated options instead of one black-box:

Option	Style	Resource Cost	Time	Stewardship
🌱 Minimal	Core change only, you do the rest	LOW	5 min	95%
🔧 Guided	Step-by-step, pause for approval each step	LOW	15 min	90%
⚡ Balanced	Proven path, full rationale	MEDIUM	25 min	80%
🔬 Experimental	Novel path, higher upside + risk	MEDIUM	40 min	varies
🌍 Steward Path	Abundance-first, history-informed	LOW	30 min	98%
Lucy marks her recommendation but never forces it. Human chooses.

Sovereignty State Machine:

AUTONOMOUS → (2 rejections) → CO_PILOT → (scaffolding trigger) → SCAFFOLDING
SCAFFOLDING → (approval streak) → CO_PILOT → (trust rebuilt) → AUTONOMOUS
